abstract: >-
  Spatia is a reproducible, open platform for subnational geospatial
  analysis of northeast Argentina (Misiones, Corrientes, Chaco, Formosa)
  and the Paraguayan departments of Itapúa and Alto Paraná, with
  buildings, census and boundaries for the rest of Paraguay and southern
  Brazil. It combines satellite imagery (Sentinel-1/2, Landsat, MODIS,
  VIIRS), census data and open geospatial datasets on an H3 hexagonal
  grid (resolution 9), from ~320,000 hexagons for Misiones to more than
  a million for Corrientes and Chaco, across 24 provinces, departments
  and states. Most layers report physical values or census rates
  directly (percent of buildings on low ground, tree cover loss rate,
  PM2.5 in ug/m3, travel minutes); the forestry layer is a
  species-distribution-model probability. The pipeline runs on Google
  Earth Engine, processes rasters into H3 zonal statistics and serves
  results via DuckDB-WASM on Cloudflare Pages. It offers 15 analyses
  across four thematic lenses: environment and risk, production and
  land, population and services, and economy and trade.
